Now tests. Need decide exact assertions and message. Let's write initial versions, then run.

`register.spec.ts`:
```ts
import { expect, test } from '../../src/fixtures/test.fixtures';

test('[AUTO-REG-01] @smoke @regression registers a new user with unique data', async ({ registerPage, header, userFactory }) => {
  const user = userFactory();
  await registerPage.open();
  await registerPage.register(user);
  await expect.poll(() => registerPage.getUrl()).toContain('/registerresult');
  await expect(registerPage.resultMessage).toHaveText('Your registration completed');
  await expect(header.accountLink).toHaveText(user.email);
  await expect(header.logoutLink).toBeVisible();
});
```
- `expect(registerPage.resultMessage).toHaveText('Your registration completed')` could fail if there's whitespace; toHaveText normalizes. Good.
- Do we need assert `getResultMessage`? The task asked add method, but test can use locator. Fine. Maybe use `expect(await registerPage.getResultMessage()).toBe('Your registration completed')` to exercise method. But web-first is better. Could do both? Not necessary. The method is available for B5. Use locator assertion.
- `header.accountLink` maybe not visible if class selector wrong; test will tell.
- After registration, URL `/registerresult`; header account. Good.

AUTO-REG-02:
```ts
test('[AUTO-REG-02] @regression validates required fields and email/password rules', async ({ registerPage }) => {
  await registerPage.open();
  await registerPage.registerButton.click();
  await expect(registerPage.firstNameInput).toBeVisible(); // not needed
  expect(await registerPage.getValidationMessages()).toEqual(expect.arrayContaining([
    'First name is required.',
    'Last name is required.',
    'Email is required.',
    'Password is required.',
  ]));
  await registerPage.firstNameInput.fill('QA');
  await registerPage.lastNameInput.fill('Automation');
  await registerPage.emailInput.fill('not-an-email');
  await registerPage.passwordInput.fill('Password123!');
  await registerPage.confirmPasswordInput.fill('Different123!');
  await registerPage.registerButton.click();
  const messages = await registerPage.getValidationMessages();
  expect(messages).toEqual(expect.arrayContaining([
    'Wrong email',
    'The password and confirmation password do not match.',
  ]));
  expect(registerPage.getUrl()).not.toContain('/registerresult');
});
```
- `getValidationMessages` after empty submit: allInnerTexts waits for locators; if no errors, returns [] immediately? It will wait for locator? `allInnerTexts` on locator with 0 elements returns [] immediately? It waits for locator resolution? Playwright locator.allInnerTexts waits for elements? It may wait until at least one? According to docs, locator.all() waits for locators to appear? `allInnerTexts` does not wait for elements? It retrieves all matching elements; if none, returns []. It might wait for actionability? Not sure. After click, server response page has errors; `allInnerTexts` likely returns them. To be safe, use `await expect(registerPage.validationErrors.first()).toBeVisible()` before getting messages. But if no errors, test fails. Could use `await expect(registerPage.validationErrors).toHaveCount(5)`? The count is 5? Empty form produced 5 (including duplicate password). But relying on 5 maybe. Better `await expect(registerPage.validationErrors.first()).toBeVisible()` then get messages. Good.
- After first submit, there are 5 errors; first visible. Then fill fields and submit; errors update. `getValidationMessages` after second submit; maybe old errors disappear/replaced. `await expect(registerPage.validationErrors.first()).toBeVisible()` again? The new errors exist. Use before get. Good.
- `expect(registerPage.getUrl()).not.toContain('/registerresult')` after invalid. Good.
- `wrong email` message might be "Wrong email" exact. Good.
- The empty form may show "Password is required." twice; arrayContaining includes one. Good.
- Could assert no `/registerresult` after empty too; final enough.
- Maybe the second submit triggers client-side validation before server; still messages. Good.

`login.spec.ts`:
```ts
import { expect, test } from '../../src/fixtures/test.fixtures';

test('[AUTO-LOGIN-01] @smoke @regression logs in with valid credentials', async ({ loginPage, header, registeredUser }) => {
  await loginPage.open();
  await loginPage.login(registeredUser.email, registeredUser.password);
  await expect.poll(() => loginPage.getUrl()).not.toContain('/login');
  await expect(header.accountLink).toHaveText(registeredUser.email);
  await expect(header.logoutLink).toBeVisible();
});

test('[AUTO-LOGIN-02] @regression rejects an incorrect password', async ({ loginPage, header, registeredUser }) => {
  await loginPage.open();
  await loginPage.login(registeredUser.email, 'WrongPassword123!');
  await expect(loginPage.errorSummary).toContainText('Login was unsuccessful. Please correct the errors and try again.');
  await expect(loginPage.errorSummary).toContainText('The credentials provided are incorrect');
  expect(loginPage.getUrl()).toContain('/login');
  await expect(header.loginLink).toBeVisible();
  await expect(header.logoutLink).not.toBeVisible();
});
```
- `expect.poll(...).not.toContain('/login')` syntax: `await expect.poll(fn).not.toContain('/login');` Playwright's expect.poll returns generic matchers; `.not` works. However `toContain` on string works. Good.
- Could use `expect.poll(() => loginPage.getUrl()).toContain('https://demowebshop.tricentis.com/')`? No, not contain /login is enough. The task says URL outside /login. Good.
- After login, header account link. If `accountLink` matches email. Good.
- After wrong password, `loginPage.getUrl()` might be `/login` with query? Contains. Good.
- `header.loginLink` visible. Good.
- `header.logoutLink` not visible. Good.
- The exact wrong password message: test asserts. If it fails, we adjust based on output. Could instead first run a one-off test to observe; but we'll run.

`cart.spec.ts`:
```ts
import { laptop } from '../../src/data/products';
import { expect, test } from '../../src/fixtures/test.fixtures';
import { parsePrice } from '../../src/utils/price';

test('[AUTO-CART-01] @smoke @regression adds a product and verifies cart totals', async ({ productPage, header, cartPage }) => {
  await productPage.open(laptop.slug);
  await productPage.setQuantity(1);
  await productPage.addToCart();

  await expect(productPage.notification).toContainText('The product has been added to your shopping cart');
  await expect(header.cartLink).toContainText('(1)');

  await cartPage.open();
  await expect(cartPage.getProductRow(laptop.name)).toBeVisible();

  const unitPrice = await cartPage.getProductPrice(laptop.name);
  expect(await cartPage.getQuantity(laptop.name)).toBe(1);
  expect(await cartPage.getLineTotal(laptop.name)).toBe(unitPrice);
  expect(parsePrice(await cartPage.getSubTotal())).toBe(unitPrice);
  expect(parsePrice(await cartPage.getTotal())).toBe(unitPrice);
});

test('[AUTO-CART-02] @regression updates quantity and recalculates totals', async ({ productPage, header, cartPage }) => {
  await productPage.open(laptop.slug);
  await productPage.setQuantity(1);
  await productPage.addToCart();
  await expect(header.cartLink).toContainText('(1)');

  await cartPage.open();
  const unitPrice = await cartPage.getProductPrice(laptop.name);

  await cartPage.updateQuantity(laptop.name, 2);
  await expect(header.cartLink).toContainText('(2)');

  expect(await cartPage.getQuantity(laptop.name)).toBe(2);
  const expectedLineTotal = Number((unitPrice * 2).toFixed(2));
  expect(await cartPage.getLineTotal(laptop.name)).toBe(expectedLineTotal);
  expect(parsePrice(await cartPage.getSubTotal())).toBe(expectedLineTotal);
  expect(parsePrice(await cartPage.getTotal())).toBe(expectedLineTotal);
});
```
- After `productPage.addToCart`, do we need wait for notification before counter? The counter expect waits. In CART-02, we don't assert notification; counter wait ensures add. Good.
- `expect(header.cartLink).toContainText('(2)')` after update; good.
- Should assert qty 2 before totals; yes.
- Could assert row visible after update; not necessary.
- `parsePrice` imported. Good.
- `getProductPrice` returns number. Good.
- No hardcoded prices. Good.
- The task says "Después de add/update, esperá el contador con expect(header.cartLink).toContainText(...) antes de leer totales." We do after add before cart open; after update before totals. Good.
- In CART-01, after add, counter wait before cart open. Good.
- Notification assertion before counter; fine.
- In CART-02, no notification assertion; task doesn't require. Fine.

